      <Placemark>
        <name>Mackinac Island</name>
        <description>Mackinac Island has no cars and is reached only by ferry. The legacy page drew it as a separate bonus marker (calcRoute('Mackinac Island, MI', 'Mackinac Island, MI', [])) with no leg, after the main loop had already closed at Ypsilanti. Verified 2026-09-26: matches Wikidata coordinate for the island within ~50m (wikidata:Q1431148). drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Shepler's Mackinac Island ferry dock in Mackinaw City (osm:node/2321023823, wikidata:Q7494519). Order fixed 2026-09-26: moved from the end of the list (where the loop ran Ann Arbor -&gt; island -&gt; Ypsilanti, adding about 500 mi that the 2015 route never drove) to between Mackinaw City and St Ignace, the ferry crossing the island lies on; the stop now adds about 1 mi and the loop closes Ann Arbor -&gt; Ypsilanti as in 2015</description>
        <styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-84.630531,45.865761,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
